# ─── Bash heredoc-leak follow-up (2026-09-03) ─────────────────────
# Catch dotted numeric / dotted module paths and other stray tokens
# that bash heredoc bugs leaked on 2026-09-03 cleanup. Files deleted:
#   root: 1,  1.0  3  None  bool  dict[str  exit  queue.Queue[tuple[str  str
#   src/ikigai/: 0.5  1.0  3  None  Taskwarrior  dict[str  list[Path]  refatoracao  str
# Listed individually — gitignore does not support `(a|b|c)` alternation
# in match patterns.
# Root-level: digit+comma, digit-dot-digit, exit, dotted module.path[...]
/[0-9],
/[0-9].[0-9]
/exit
/queue.*\[*
# src/ikigai/ depth: broaden `list[dict[...` to all `list[...]`, plus
# Taskwarrior and refatoracao (PT-BR lowercase; bash > refatoracao leak)
src/ikigai/[0-9].[0-9]
src/ikigai/[0-9]
src/ikigai/Taskwarrior
src/ikigai/IntentClassification
src/ikigai/dict
src/ikigai/list\[*
src/ikigai/refatoracao

# ─── Bash heredoc-leak follow-up (2026-09-04) ─────────────────────
# Stray tokens from sub-agent runs: paren-wrapped calls (`agent('Execute')`),
# paren-balancing close fragments (`'))]+`), bare English words (`The`,
# `first`, `StateGraph`), multi-digit (`10`), and pydantic-version-like
# tokens (`2.13.5\``).
# Each listed individually because gitignore lacks alternation support.
/agent('Execute')`
/'))]+
/The
/first
/StateGraph
/[0-9][0-9]
/[0-9][0-9][0-9]

