# Stray root-level files from bash heredoc-leak patterns (2026-09-05).
# PascalCase identifier (`Static`, 0 bytes) and lowercase word (`empty`,
# 0 bytes) — same root-cause class as existing /None /str /int /Path
# patterns in the heredoc-leak sections above.
# Cleanup is via `rm Static empty` in the closeout commit; these
# patterns prevent recurrence.
/Static
/empty
# Backtick-wrapped expression fragments (e.g. `Proposal(approval_state`,
# `agent('Execute')`) — bash > word with leading backticks leaks
# unquoted paren content as a 0-byte filename.
/``*
# .swarm/ state files written by claude-flow at runtime. state.json is
# the only one tracked (older intent). Add backups/ + JSON state files
# so they don't get picked up if the loose track pattern is broadened.
.swarm/backups/
.swarm/model-router-state.json
# SQLite WAL-mode artifacts emitted alongside .swarm/*.db at runtime —
# ignored so they don't get tracked on every daemon tick. Mirror pattern
# at the canonical db-root location (data/) is already in place via
# data/*.db + data/chroma_db/ + data/review_queue/ above.
.swarm/*.db-shm
.swarm/*.db-wal
# Stray root-level zero-byte file from bash heredoc leak (same root
# cause as /Static /empty /None /str above; cleanup via `rm word`).
# Recurrence prevention: pattern locks it out if the redirect recurs.
/word
# Loop engineering runtime logs — generated on each loop-tick run, would
# accumulate unbounded if tracked. Scaffolding (loop-tick.sh, roadmap,
# tasks, progress, specs) IS tracked; only the log output is ignored.
.claude/loop/logs/

# ─── Bash heredoc-leak follow-up (2026-09-07) ─────────────────────
# Stray root-level files from bash redirect leaks during M0/M1 loop
# scaffolding work: `80%` (0-byte from `> 80%` redirect) and `c` (251-byte
# heredoc fragment from `awk ... OVER_BUDGET ... > c`). Same root-cause
# class as /Static /empty /None /str /int /Path above.
# Cleanup: `rm 80% c` in closeout commit.
# Prevention: bash redirections should use `cmd > file.txt 2>&1` style;
# bare `> word` with shell-special chars leaks the literal.
/80%
/c
# ─── Bash heredoc-leak follow-up (2026-09-07 cont.) ─────────────
# Two more stray root-level files from this session's loop wiring work:
# `c'` (0-byte, trailing single quote) and `word`` (0-byte, trailing
# backtick). Same root-cause class — bare `> word'` or `> word\`` leaks
# the literal including trailing shell-special chars. Cleanup via `rm`.
# Also add .worktrees/ safety pattern (only registered worktrees should
# exist; stale dirs on disk need PendingFileRenameOperations on Windows
# reboot per the windows-orphan-dir-delete memory).
/c'
/word`
/.worktrees/
